  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">-- This/these answers have been migrated from a previous version of Trac --
The SAfAIDS SCORE intervention&apos;s overall aim to contribute to a sustained 50% reduction in new infections and improved positive sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) outcomes for communities in southern Africa by 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SAfAIDS har ans&#xf6;kt om 40 000 000 SEK i bidrag till genomf&#xf6;randet av det 5-&#xe5;riga programmet &#x201d;Sustainable Communities of Real Excellence (SCORE)&#x201d; i s&#xf6;dra Afrika (Lesotho, Malawi, Sydafrika, Swaziland, Zambia och Zimbabwe) under perioden 2014-2018. Syftet &#xe4;r att fram till 2018 bidra till en halvering av nya HIV- infektioner samt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter (SRHR) i samh&#xe4;llen i s&#xf6;dra Afrika.
Det svenska bidraget f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;s att vara i form av k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d och kommer finansiera verksamhet inom programmet under perioden 1 juli 2014 - 30 juni 2017.

Projektf&#xf6;rslaget inneh&#xe5;ller tre strategiska m&#xe5;l:
1. Motverka hiv, tuberkulos och k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld samt fr&#xe4;mja tillg&#xe5;ng SRHR bland unga mellan 10-24 &#xe5;r i s&#xf6;dra Afrika.
2. &#xd6;ka tillg&#xe5;ngen till tj&#xe4;nster som hanterar SRH, hiv, tuberkulos och k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld f&#xf6;r marginaliserade kvinnor mellan 25-49 &#xe5;r i s&#xf6;dra Afrika 
3. Fr&#xe4;mja diskriminerade gruppers (hbt-personer, personer som lever med hiv, sexarbetare och f&#xe5;ngar) m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter i syfte att f&#xf6;rebygga hiv, tuberkulos, k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld och homofobi genom att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra tillg&#xe5;ngen till icke-stigmatiserande SRHR information och service.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAfAIDS has applied to Sida for funding of 40 000 000 SEK to carry out the five year program &quot;Sustainable Communities of Real Excellence&quot; (SCORE) in southern Africa (Lesotho, Malawi, South Africa, Swaziland, Zambia and Zimbabwe) during the period 2014-2018. 
The Swedish contribution is proposed to be core support and cover activities during the period from July 1, 2014 until June 30, 2017.

The intervention aims at contributing to a sustained 50% reduction in new infections and improved positive sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) outcomes for communities in southern Africa by 2018. The program has three core strategic objectives:
1. Promote access to strategic, evidence-based HIV, TB, SGBV prevention and SRH&amp;R information and services that enhance preventative behaviors and demand for SRH services by young people aged 10-24 years (in and out of schools, in prisons and informal settlements surrounding mines) in Southern Africa by 2018.
2. Scale up SRH&amp;R interventions that promote prevention of HIV, TB and SGBV and enhance referrals and uptake of key SRH services for vulnerable women 25-49 years (in prisons and informal settlements surrounding mines) in Southern Africa by 2018. 
3. Promote the rights of key populations (LGBTI, people living with HIV (PLHIV), prisoners and sex workers) to prevent HIV, TB, SGBV, and homophobia to enhance access to non stigmatized SRHR information and services</narrative>
  </description>
